From 36dae97fa81fcd3c60a69370c289b02eb59f28bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taimoor Ul Islam <tislam@iastate.edu>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 16:44:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 15/52] kaiair: PktR live control-file overlay, GUI can toggle
 power/gamma without restart

Co-design step 2. Adds an optional runtime overlay to pktr_runtime_config: when
KAIAIR_PKTR_CTRL_FILE is set, the demo-critical toggles (power actuation on/off,
SINR-target margin gamma) are re-read from the agent's JSON control file at
runtime (rate-limited ~2 Hz via atomics) so the AgSlicing GUI can flip PktR on a
running gNB. When the env var is unset (all non-GUI runs + unit tests) the overlay
never activates and behaviour is identical to the env-only path (backward compat).

- pktr_actuate_now()/pktr_gamma_now(): live-effective accessors (fall back to env)
- UL gate (pktr_ul_sinr_offset_db) and DL loop (pktr_dl_power_controller update/
  pwr_ctrl_offset) consult the overlay; metrics view shows live UL-actuate + gamma

Verified on HW: UL-actuate off->ON->off and gamma 3.0->8.0 dB, live via the API
with an attached UE, no restart. Unit tests unchanged (7+9+5 pass).
